Warning ('test-multivariate-engine-parity.R:153:3'): Tier B1/B2: the bridge reproduces the serialized k=2 target element-wise
The data have repeated records per individual (80 records for 20 individuals), but the model has no `permanent(1 | ...)` term. The additive variance will ABSORB the permanent-environment variance, so `animal` and the heritability derived from it are inflated -- they are not narrow-sense quantities here.
To identify Va vs Vpe on a multi-trait repeated-measures model, add `permanent(1 | <id>)` to the cbind() formula (hsquared#237; experimental; public_covered_count stays 7):
  hsquared(
    cbind(<t1>, <t2>) ~ <fixed> + animal(1 | <id>, pedigree = ped) + permanent(1 | <id>),
    data = <data>
  )
